Validates json syntax

Usage: jjp check [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --parser <PARSER>
          Parser to use for input

          Possible values:
          - json:      A single json document
          - jsonc:     A single json document with comments and trailing commas
          - jsonlines: One json document per line
          
          [default: json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
	$ echo -en "{\"hello I am valid\": null} " | jjp check

	$ echo -en "{\"coolKey\"}" | jjp check
	error: expected colon after key, found `}`
	 --> stdin:1:11
	  |
	1 | {"coolKey"}
	  |  ---------^
	  |  |
	  |  expected due to `"coolKey"`
	  |
	help: insert colon and placeholder value
	  |
	1 | {"coolKey": "🐟🛹"}
	  |           ++++++++

